From 67f83c13a594a712a2c868a0b3c7082a6754e2cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:00:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: F-219 - drag by backpedalling in melee (facing the mob,
 still swinging)

- move: MoveToRequest.backward - face away from the travel direction, MSG_MOVE_START_BACKWARD,
  BACKWARD-flagged heartbeats, run-back speed (4.5 yd/s scaled with run speed)
- combat: KillRequest drag_x/y/z + drag_when_spent; once the target is in melee and we swing, back-
  pedal to the drag point and fight on (KillResult.drags). Casters (drag_when_spent) only once no
  offensive spell is castable; hunters and melee on melee contact - no shot or cast is traded
- runner: drag_clear picks the spot (12-28 yd, walk crossing no other mob's reach) and hands it to
  the first defend fight instead of turning and running (7 of the rogue's 9 deaths followed that)
Live, Eversong rogue 30 min: 5 drag plans, 4 dragged fights, all killed, 14-26 swings while
backing off; 1 death in the half hour (not a dragged fight).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019SSuH6gpqY4Kn5Rk9sd149
